use ../../../lib/UiComponent

export ui-component TextField:
    description:
        A text field is a box for typing a single line of text. It can show a
        hint while empty, and can be set up for special kinds of text such as
        passwords, email addresses, or searches.

    label:
        A text field always has a name, normally shown as a visible label. The
        hint shown while it's empty (the placeholder) is not a label and
        disappears as soon as the user types.

    value:
        The text the user has typed. The component using the field is told
        each time it changes, and can also set it.

    kinds:
        The field can be marked as a particular kind of text, such as a
        password, email address, phone number, web address, or search. This
        lets the platform help, for example by showing a suitable on-screen
        keyboard, or hiding a password as it's typed. Which kinds exist, and
        how each is handled, is up to the chosen library.

    restrictions:
        The component can limit what can be typed, such as a maximum length
        or only certain characters.

    helpAndErrors:
        The field can show help text, and an error message when what was
        typed isn't valid. Both are linked to the field so assistive tools read
        them out with it. Deciding what's valid is up to the component or
        form, not the field.

    extras:
        The field can show something fixed before or after the text, such as a
        currency sign or unit, and may have a button to clear it.

    disabled:
        A disabled field can't be focused or changed. A read-only field can't
        be changed, but can still be focused, and its text selected and copied.

    nonGoals:
        - Only one line. For several lines, use a TextArea
        - It doesn't decide what's valid. It only shows the error it's given
